WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.810
The one piece manga just confirmed one of
the most popular theories which is that Blackbeard

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:08.290
absolutely can eat a third devil fruit.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:13.580
And this mind-blowing reveal comes with massive
implications for the story as Blackbeard considers

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:18.100
whether or not to eat the Ope Ope no mi after
defeating Trafalgar Law.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:23.720
And even though Law escapes, we now know that
Blackbeard will surely be hunting for a third

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:28.830
supremely powerful devil fruit to pair with
his strongest devil fruits in the story.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:34.490
And that’s not the only epic clash in this
chapter as we get confirmation that the former

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:41.410
marine admiral Aokiji is actually one of Blackbeard’s
titanic captains and he is on Pirate Island

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:45.110
RIGHT NOW to stop Garp from rescuing Koby.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:51.989
But that is not going to be an easy feat,
as we get even more evidence that Garp is

00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:54.890
the most insanely powerful marine in the story.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:01:00.399
And if that wasn’t enough, we learn even
more clues about Aokiji's mysterious time

00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:05.650
after leaving the marines and more hints about
where the elusive fourth Road Poneglyph might

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:06.790
be.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:09.670
Starting with the epic conclusion to Law versus
Blackbeard.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:14.380
In chapter 1063, we first see Law and Blackbeard
clash on Winner Island.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:21.220
And in this all out battle Law used his god-like
devil fruit to fend off the darkness and earthquake

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.360
wielding Blackbeard.

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:28.540
But the fighting has finally reached its conclusion
as we see a bloodied and panting Blackbeard

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.290
standing over a defeated Law.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:35.240
And in this scene we seem to get as close
to an answer as we’ve ever had to one of

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.869
the biggest mysteries in all of One Piece.

00:01:38.869 --> 00:01:43.850
Ever since Marineford when Blackbeard did
the unthinkable and took Whitebeard’s devil

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:49.469
fruit for himself, we have always wondered
if he would be able to eat a third devil fruit.

00:01:49.469 --> 00:01:56.259
And the answer seems to be yes, as Blackbeard
openly wonders if he should take Law’s powers

00:01:56.259 --> 00:02:00.780
and use them or sell the coveted Ope-Ope no
mi to the highest bidder.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:05.740
And while he doesn’t outright say that he
wants to eat it, we can basically assume that

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:10.330
he is talking about himself for a few reasons.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:17.650
First, all of his other titanic captains already
have devil fruits, so unless anyone can eat

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.670
two fruits, that rules out all of them.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:25.700
And I really don’t think Blackbeard would
give it to just some random member of his

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:30.610
crew, so that really only leaves himself as
an option to eat the fruit.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:38.390
But if he decided to sell it, one group who
would definitely be interested in the fruit

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:39.720
is the World Government.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:45.180
We’ve known they’ve been after this fruit
since we saw them try so hard to obtain it

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.700
during Law’s heart-breaking flashback.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.530
And then during the last chapter we learned
that Blackbeard wants to officially join the

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:53.640
world government as a kingdom.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:03:00.980
So maybe he could trade the Ope fruit in exchange
for membership in the world government.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:08.610
But whether he wanted to eat it or trade Law’s
fruit, this mind-blowing reveal brings up

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:14.450
the old question of how exactly can Blackbeard
eat more than one devil fruit.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:19.180
We don’t get any clues that anyone else
in his crew is able to do this, so it truly

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:22.860
seems that this ability is specific to Blackbeard.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:24.780
But why is that?

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:29.709
Personally, I’m dying to know, but a few
theories we have discussed before on the channel

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:34.739
are that Blackbeard has multiple personalities
or that there is something weird about his

00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:37.319
body that allows him to eat multiple devil
fruits.

00:03:37.319 --> 00:03:44.189
Or it could be some super secret power of
the darkness fruit that we don’t yet know

00:03:44.189 --> 00:03:45.340
about.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:51.500
It is also unclear if Blackbeard would need
to kill Law in order to take his devil fruit,

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.450
as Law is clearly still alive in this chapter.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:04:00.280
And every time we have seen devils fruits
taken or talked about being taken, it involved

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.870
someone needing to be killed.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:05.670
For example, with Whitebeard’s death in
Marineford and when Burgess wanted to take

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:07.670
Luffy’s fruit in Dressrosa.

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:13.720
But while Blackbeard takes his time deciding
what to do, this scene takes a WILD turn of

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:14.720
events.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:20.290
Law’s loyal mink polar bear, Bepo, takes
a mysterious drug which allows him to enter

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:21.820
the mink’s most ferociously powerful form:
Sulong.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:26.340
And normally this form can only be used during
the full moon, but apparently this drug that

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:30.509
was developed by Chopper allows them to enter
the form whenever they want.

00:04:30.509 --> 00:04:35.940
Which is so interesting because we are getting
more evidence that Chopper is truly becoming

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:38.530
a medical genius.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:48.880
And in this beastly form, Bepo is able to
steal Law away and escape into the sea, leaving

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.940
the other members of Law’s crew abandoned
on the island.

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:57.820
Which leaves us with a super interesting question:
Where does Law go from here?

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:00.870
There are many possible options.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:06.540
First, Egghead island should be somewhat close
by, since Law and Luffy both came to these

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:09.160
islands directly after leaving Wano.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:14.070
So it’s possible that Bepo will take Law
to Egghead where they will encounter the Straw

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.070
Hat pirates.

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:20.130
And even though Law and Luffy declared their
alliance over I could see Law asking for Luffy’s

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.240
help if it meant saving his crew.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:33.539
Another option, and one that personally has
me extremely excited, is that Bepo could take

00:05:33.539 --> 00:05:36.430
Law to his home, Zou.

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:41.960
This would bring the enormous walking elephant
Zunesha back into the story as we only saw

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:44.490
it for a brief few chapters when it came to
Wano.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:49.760
Clearly, Zunesha still has some role to play
in the story, so this could be one way to

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:52.360
reintroduce the massive elephant once again.

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:57.569
And even more exciting is the entire country
of minks living on Zunesha’s back.

00:05:57.569 --> 00:06:05.650
With this new drug that can let Minks go sulong
whenever they choose, this entire country

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:10.440
who are allies with Luffy, just got way way
stronger.

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:16.690
We already saw in Wano that sulong minks can
be devastating fighters, so a whole army of

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:22.420
these ferocious animals would be insanely
powerful for the battles to come.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:27.090
And there is no greater upcoming battle than
the race to find the one piece.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:34.349
With Law defeated, we can assume that Blackbeard
has taken his copies of the Road Poneglyphs

00:06:34.349 --> 00:06:37.650
which are necessary to reach Laugh Tale.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:42.440
And we did a full breakdown of who has which
Road poneglyphs in a recent chapter review,

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:48.150
but basically this means Blackbeard now has
at least two of the Road Poneglyphs, and as

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:53.360
we will discuss in just a few minutes, he
is likely to get at least one more very soon.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:57.690
But now that Law is defeated, this means that
the final players in the race to find the

00:06:57.690 --> 00:06:59.780
One Piece are now set.

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:05.840
Law and Captain Kid, who was just defeated
by Shanks, are no longer serious contenders,

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:12.690
which just leaves Luffy, Shanks, Blackbeard,
AND THE MOST IMPORTANT character, Buggy.

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:19.080
Come on, you can never leave Buggy out of
these kinds of important events.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:24.450
But now we have to ask what will Blackbeard
do next?

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:27.970
Will he pursue another strong devil fruit
to take as his own?

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:31.180
Or just move onto whatever his next objective
is?

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:36.759
And if he is going hunting for a third devil
fruit, we have to ask which power does Blackbeard

00:07:36.759 --> 00:07:37.759
want?

00:07:37.759 --> 00:07:44.169
Well, in this chapter, we get a hint that
he isn’t dead set on a particular devil

00:07:44.169 --> 00:07:45.940
fruit to eat as his third power.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:51.380
It seems he wasn’t sure if he wanted the
Ope fruit for himself or not, so maybe he

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:56.699
is still undecided or simply waiting to see
what supremely overpowered devil fruit he

00:07:56.699 --> 00:07:57.800
can get his hands on.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:03.090
But it is certainly possible that he chases
after Law and Bepo to take back the Ope powers,

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:08.150
but if he can’t do that there are some other
options for fruits that he could want.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:13.300
And personally, it has never really made sense
for him to eat another Logia as I don’t

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:16.830
know how he could be darkness AND another
element at the same time.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:21.050
So that leaves a Zoan power or a Parameica.

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:25.099
So there are a few strong Zoans Blackbeard
could target.

00:08:25.099 --> 00:08:29.110
With Kaido defeated, Blackbeard could be after
his mythical devil fruit.

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:34.430
Or, with Kaido not ruling over Wano, Blackbeard
could sneak in and go after the two other

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:36.580
mythical fruits still on the island.

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:41.440
Those are Momo’s version of the dragon fruit
and Yamato’s Okuchi no Makami fruit, which

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:44.310
lets her turn into this wolf guardian deity.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:48.890
And Blackbeard sneaking into this territory
would make sense because we just saw them

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:52.890
sneak into Big Mom’s territory to kidnap
Big Mom’s daughter.

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:57.560
Besides Wano, there is currently a large gathering
of strong devil fruit users on Egghead.

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:03.260
So Blackbeard could join the epic conflict
in order to steal some devil fruits such as

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:07.640
the Leopard fruit or, even Stussy’s unnamed
vampire-like fruit.

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:14.760
It is also entirely possible that Vegapunk
has a storehouse of strong devil fruits that

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:16.470
could be taken during the fighting.

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:20.670
And of course there are also the Straw Hat’s
devil fruits that Blackbeard could have his

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:21.670
eye on.

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:27.660
And speaking of Straw Hats, has anyone else
noticed that it has now been three whole chapters

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:30.890
since we have even seen our main characters?

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:36.820
How crazy is that in the middle of an arc?

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:45.440
But personally I’m not complaining since
we keep getting these incredible chapters

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:50.510
of events outside of Egghead.

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:55.019
But if Blackbeard doesn’t chase Law or go
to one of the other islands I just mentioned,

00:09:55.019 --> 00:10:00.570
the most likely option is that he returns
to his home base, Pirate Island, to join the

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:06.959
earth shattering conflict between the increasingly
badass Garp and his former pupil, Kuzan.

00:10:06.959 --> 00:10:13.600
And this clash will undoubtedly have a massive
effect on the future of the Blackbeard pirate

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:16.029
which we will discuss in full detail in just
a moment.

00:10:16.029 --> 00:10:21.079
But one note is that since Kuzan is no longer
an admiral, we won’t use his admiral nickname

00:10:21.079 --> 00:10:27.540
Aokiji anymore, and instead call him by his
actual name Kuzan.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:33.610
But before we get to that titanic fight, we
see a flashback about the first time that

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:35.889
Kuzan met with Blackbeard.

00:10:35.889 --> 00:10:41.610
We are told this event is about one year after
Kuzan lost his devastating, island-warping

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:44.920
battle against the current fleet admiral Akainu.

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:49.970
After this battle Kuzan left the marines because
he couldn’t stand taking orders from Akainu.

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:55.410
We aren’t told what Kuzan has been doing
in between that fight and this scene in the

00:10:55.410 --> 00:11:01.300
flashback, but there are a number of hints
we can use to try and figure it out.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:06.450
In chapter 698 we see Kuzan for the very first
time after the time skip when he saves Vice-admiral

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:08.070
Smoker on Punk Hazard.

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:12.530
And in this conversation, Kuzan’s clothes
suggest that he is still wandering as a loner

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:14.700
and has not yet joined the Blackbeard pirates.

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:19.910
I mean, just look at the differences between
this outfit and these that he is wearing as

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:23.290
one of Blackbeard’s titanic captains.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:28.810
Clearly something changed in the few months
since Punk Hazard.

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:34.622
However, Blackbeard could have offered for
Kuzan to join him halfway through the two

00:11:34.622 --> 00:11:40.500
year time skip but Kuzan might have taken
a while before accepting the offer to join

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:42.170
the Emperor’s crew.

00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:48.480
Regardless, it is clear Kuzan has been acting
on his own for sometime during and after the

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:53.480
timeskip, which makes me wonder what exactly
he was doing.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:57.350
Blackbeard even said in this chapter that
pirates can still have their own agenda’s,

00:11:57.350 --> 00:12:02.310
so maybe Blackbeard just let’s Kuzan do
whatever he wants unless directly ordered

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:04.860
by Blackbeard.

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:09.600
But the clearest answer to all of this speculation,
and the one most people expect, is that he

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:14.550
has resigned from the marines and joined the
secret marine organization, Sword.

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:19.600
We just learned in chapter 1080 that all the
members of Sword are former marines who are

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:24.400
no longer affiliated with the world government
so that they can act on their own behalf.

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:30.270
Basically they are like Garp, who pretty much
does whatever he wants.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:35.350
And the evidence for Kuzan being a member
of Sword is made even clearer when we compare

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:42.019
some of Kuzan’s dialogue from chapter 699
to what we just learned in the last chapter.

00:12:42.019 --> 00:12:45.050
Take a look at what Kuzan says while talking
to Smoker.

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:49.710
First, he states that “You don’t have
to be affiliated with the Navy to accomplish

00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:55.339
things” and that “There are some things
you can only see when you remain independent”.

00:12:55.339 --> 00:13:03.139
That is also exactly how Sword was described
in chapter 1080, so it makes complete sense

00:13:03.139 --> 00:13:10.040
that he is acting on his own beliefs as a
member of Sword.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:14.500
At the end of his conversation with Smoker,
he even warns the vice-admiral about the dangers

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:19.730
of Doflamingo in Dressrosa and then went on
to tell the marines to not reveal that they

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:20.730
had seen him.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:24.690
And it makes sense that he would only care
about these things if, one, he was a part

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:29.561
of the secret marine organization, and, two,
he planned to go undercover and didn’t want

00:13:29.561 --> 00:13:33.570
Blackbeard finding out that he was still helping
the marines?

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:40.110
So personally it all lines up that he infiltrated
Blackbeard’s crew with some intention of

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:44.420
betraying Blackbeard.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:51.820
But back to the flashback we see in this chapter,
Blackbeard arrives on the scene and three

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:56.380
of his titanic captains are already frozen
by Kuzan’s ice powers.

00:13:56.380 --> 00:14:00.470
And while one of Blackbeard’s allies thinks
it would be best to kill Kuzan right away,

00:14:00.470 --> 00:14:07.490
they instead have a jolly old time drinking
and having fun inside the bar.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:15.320
And maybe Kuzan has changed since joining
the marines, but this is certainly not the

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:19.500
laid-back, lazy, and emotionless dude that
we are used to.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:25.300
Which makes me think even more that this is
an act that he is putting on to fool Blackbeard.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:29.570
And eventually Blackbeard asks Kuzan about
the man with the burn scar because he thinks

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:34.920
that this person might have the final Road
Poneglyph.

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:38.670
And this was a TRULY MASSIVE SHOCK when I
read this.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:42.480
I mean, we barely learned about this mysterious
figure in chapter 1056.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.959
Captain Kid knew about him and his connection
to the One Piece.

00:14:45.959 --> 00:14:52.360
But if the Blackbeard crew knew about him
over a year ago, just how secretive is this

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:53.360
guy?

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:58.389
Well, we got more information about who this
might be in chapter 1066.

00:14:58.389 --> 00:15:02.580
We learned that the giant former marine Saul,
who we thought was killed during the destruction

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:05.200
of Ohara, was most likely alive.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:10.520
So it makes a lot of sense that he is the
man marked by flames, since he literally was

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:16.800
running through flames, he could have ice
burns after being frozen by Kuzan, and we

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:20.089
see him wrapped in bandages in this panel
right here.

00:15:20.089 --> 00:15:24.250
And since Saul was connected to the incident
at Ohara, and those same scholars were studying

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:29.790
the Poneglyphs, it would be logical that Saul
could be protecting the final Road Poneglyph.

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:34.860
Plus We already know from Vegapunk’s flashback
that the giants of Elbaf salvaged everything

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:40.241
they could from Ohara, so it would certainly
be reasonable for the final Road Poneglyph

00:15:40.241 --> 00:15:42.840
to be on Elbaf with Saul.

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:48.880
And while Kuzan denies knowing anything about
the man marked by flames or the final Road

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:57.420
Poneglyph, he could just be lying to protect
Saul, since Saul was a friend of Kuzan’s.

00:15:57.420 --> 00:16:01.300
And yet another rumor that is hinted at in
this scene is that the man marked by flames

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:05.880
travels on a black ship and has some ability
to create whirlpools.

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:12.279
And a black ship makes me think of this ship,
which was captained by Rocks D. Xebec.

00:16:12.279 --> 00:16:16.540
Another option is that it could be referring
to the leader of the Revolutionary army, Monkey

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:17.860
D. Dragon.

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:23.240
Whirlpools can be formed by strong winds,
and we know Dragon has some kind of wind powers,

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:26.990
since he basically always is accompanied by
strong winds whenever he appears in the story.

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:31.560
Plus, we found out recently that Dragon also
had ties to the scholars of Ohara, so it is

00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:42.540
possible that Dragon and Saul became allies
after the events of Ohara.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:46.519
But all of this makes me wonder how anyone
knows about the man marked by flames in the

00:16:46.519 --> 00:16:47.550
first place.

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:52.480
If this person is Saul, then he should have
been in hiding for literally decades.

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:56.630
But somehow Blackbeard and even Kid had heard
rumors about him.

00:16:56.630 --> 00:17:00.209
So are there traitors within the giants of
Elbaf?

00:17:00.209 --> 00:17:07.150
Or is this mysterious figure someone completely
different that we haven’t met yet?

00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:12.569
Whatever the answer, it will certainly be
just as exciting as the mouth-watering clash

00:17:12.569 --> 00:17:16.439
between Kuzan and Garp on pirate island.

00:17:16.439 --> 00:17:21.980
We first see Kuzan freeze Koby’s friend
and then after a brief bit of dialogue, Kuzan

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:26.699
freezes Garp with an Ice Ball attack, just
like he did against Whitebeard during Marineford.

00:17:26.699 --> 00:17:32.050
And just like his legendary former rival,
Garp easily breaks out of the ice,&nbsp; and in

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:39.100
a burst of blinding speed, Garb grabs Kuzan’s
face in a haki-covered fist and slams him

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:44.250
into the ground with such tremendous power
that it reminds me of all the ground shattering

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:48.570
attacks Luffy has used to defeat his opponents
over the years.

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:55.799
And besides the fighting, there is a ton to
unpack from the brief dialogue between the

00:17:55.799 --> 00:17:56.799
two.

00:17:56.799 --> 00:18:01.770
Before they clash, Kuzan reveals that he was
actually trained by Garp sometime in the past.

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:06.520
This lends even more evidence to the theory
that Kuzan is secretly a member of Sword,

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:11.790
since Koby and Helmeppo are both members of
Sword and they were both trained by Garp.

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:18.450
And maybe this is just crazy copium on my
part because he certainly doesn’t look friendly

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:19.490
during this clash.

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:25.550
Seriously, if he is secretly undercover, then
he is putting a painful amount of effort into

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:30.700
convincing the Blackbeard pirates that he
is still on his side.

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:39.169
And while it appears that Garp has the advantage
in this epic battle, we simply never know

00:18:39.169 --> 00:18:40.280
with fights in One Piece.

00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:44.320
And this could turn around very quickly.

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:48.429
Maybe Kuzan isn’t taking this fight seriously
yet, or maybe the other Blackbeard titanic

00:18:48.429 --> 00:18:51.220
captains will come in and together overwhelm
Garp.

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:57.470
Or maybe Garp will once again prove that he
is the strongest marine, and wipe them all

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:58.470
out anyway.

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:02.590
But that’s not all that we learn from this
legendary battle.

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:07.270
Since Kuzan is now confirmed to be here on
Pirate Island, this information partially

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:09.679
solves a mystery from chapter 1079.

00:19:09.679 --> 00:19:15.549
For a single panel in that chapter, we saw
that one of Blackbeard’s ships is currently

00:19:15.549 --> 00:19:17.799
just outside of Egghead island.

00:19:17.799 --> 00:19:22.220
Previously I thought that this might be Kuzan
since it would make sense for him to join

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:26.520
a conflict with the world government, but
that is clearly not the case.

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:32.630
Since Kuzan is on pirate island, we now have
a pretty good idea of who is coming to Egghead.

00:19:32.630 --> 00:19:36.400
Right now on Pirate island we have these five
titanic captains.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:39.500
And currently accompanying Blackbeard are
these three.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:43.330
Which only leaves Laffitte and Caterina Devon.

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:49.890
And honestly, it makes perfect sense for them
to be the ones coming to Egghead because there

00:19:49.890 --> 00:19:54.630
is no one better at sneaking around on the
Blackbeard crew than these two.

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:59.660
We already know that Laffitte is super stealthy
as he even managed to sneak into Mary Geoise,

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:04.100
he has some hypnosis powers, and he can fly
with his wings.

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:08.870
But even better for trickery is Caterina Devon,
who has the shape-shifting powers of the mythical

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:10.720
Nine-Tailed fox devil fruit.

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:15.500
So together, these two form the perfect pair
to steal into the chaos of Egghead island

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:17.580
and take whatever they want.

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:21.740
It could be the copies of the Road Poneglyphs
on the Straw Hats ship, or it could be that

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:25.809
they have their eyes on a super strong devil
fruit that they want to capture if someone

00:20:25.809 --> 00:20:26.809
dies.

00:20:26.809 --> 00:20:33.240
But with one conflict wrapping up, and the
others getting even more incredible by the

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:38.669
chapters, I cannot wait to see who comes out
on top in these world-changing battles.

00:20:38.669 --> 00:20:43.520
And if you want to know why the godly powers
of Garp will completely change the rest of

00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:47.500
the story, you can watch this video right
here.

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:49.550
Shanks for watching.

